Heh; I wrote our own game recorder several years ago, before I'd heard 
of any standardly-used ones.  Hopefully that will get changed this year, 
but maybe not.

We do allow NetHack to run suid and to manage its own files on the game 
server just as it would on a normal installation.

We use the logfile, instead of the scores file; it has way more info 
available in it, and we also use Aardvark's extended logfile patch.  The 
logfiles from each game server are collected by the control server every 
10 minutes and new entries are imported into the database.  The 
Tournament scoreboard is generated as a static HTML file from the 
database every 10 minutes.

